  "id": "profiling",
  "term": "profiling",
  "definition": "Profiling, in this biological context, means measuring patterns of metabolites to detect changes in cellular activity and to help identify biomarkers linked to disease processes. It compares metabolite patterns across samples, often using analytical methods such as mass spectrometry or NMR together with statistical analysis to find meaningful group differences.",
